{"availability":"available","full":"Kyn21kx/ImWebGui","name":"ImWebGui","description":"A small C++ template project to develop native WASM applications with ImGui for interfaces","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-07-28T05:22:15Z","updated":"2024-08-27T06:30:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://tweet2doom.github.io/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.271Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.271Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.271Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.271Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Template for making a GUI app with C++ / Dear ImGui / SDL / OpenGL / Emscripten that can run both natively and in the browser.","This is a startup project for creating C++ GUI applications that can run both as a native app and as a web app. This is achieved by compiling the C++ code to WebAssembly using Emscripten. The project uses Dear ImGui + OpenGL backend to draw stuff on the screen. The project provides basic functionality needed for most apps:","When running natively, the app creates an SDL window and renders stuff using OpenGL. When running as a web app, it runs in a WebGL canvas."],"features":["Create and initialize an SDL window with OpenGL context","Basic single-threaded Render/Update loop","Basic HTML boilerplate for running the app in a web page","Interface for passing data between C++ and Javascript","Copy text to clipboard"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kyn21kx/ImWebGui/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"26166cc54d91c9936ad7974705814ab70f3cc38375596bace50f0cf4fcc74454","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.461Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:58.461Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Template for making a GUI app with C++ / Dear ImGui / SDL / OpenGL / Emscripten that can run both natively and in the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://git